                        <p>RJennings, Edmund 29.1.1789 Jennings at B Hollis' /
                            30.5.1789, 4.11.1789, 27.1.1790, 21.12.1790, 2.3.1791, 11.4.1791,
                            14.7.1791, 9.1.1792 and 31.3.1792 there / 2.6.1797 Jennings at B Hollis'
                            / 22.6.1798 meet E Jennings Edmund Jenings, mentioned in Brand Hollis'
                            will (PCC 1804) and present at most of Brand Hollis' dinners when Godwin
                            dined there. Wrote a work on the peace with America 1778 and a dispute
                            with Henry Laurens 1783. In 1791 listed as member of Unitarian Society,
                            address Wright's Hotel, Soho Sq. On 13.6.1792 he chaired meeting at
                            London Tavern of Society for Commemorating the Glorious… </p>
